      "relevantCases": [
        "allows an unowned harness and proves terminal owner rows are excluded by goal status",
        "allows the active goal that owns the target harness",
        "refuses placement when a different active goal owns the target harness",
        "a LIVE owner (non-terminal worklist plan) refuses and never pays for the oracle",
        "an owner whose only worklist plan is terminal (count 0) with a DEAD holder is vacant",
        "a STANDING goal is not released by a recorded disposition alone",
        "measures the worklist over non-archived, non-terminal plans using the plan grammar",
        "reads the arm from the goal row and fails soft toward full on a read error",
        "rejects a non-positive ceiling — 0 agents is a paused goal, not a launch policy",
        "accepts a holder policy on the settings document",
        "REJECTS an unknown key inside the holder policy too — .strict() on BOTH levels",
        "rejects an onLoss value outside the closed set, so a typo cannot read as a policy",
        "accepts null on either field and on the policy itself — the panel clears with null",
        "covers a goal that has pinned NOTHING — the case the defaults exist for",
        "defaults onLoss to deactivate — a goal earns respawn only by being NAMED (D-001)",
        "REFUSES a goal that declares nothing (the case the item exists for)",
        "ADMITS a goal that pinned only onLoss — engaging with the policy IS declaring it",
        "REFUSES a null-cleared policy — clearing is unpinning, not opting out",
        "CONTROL: the rule reads requireLive, so an opted-out goal is admitted even unpinned elsewhere",
        "lets an explicit caller request beat the stored policy",
        "returns an empty profile when a goal has no settings at all",
        "accepts every slot the GOAL contract enumerates",
        "isGoalLaunchRole separates a slot from a persona",
        "refuses ceilings below the floor on a goal that runs a drain fleet, and writes nothing",
        "allows the same ceilings on a sole-member goal (no drain fleet)",
        "does not read the goal row when the new ceilings already clear the floor",
        "fails CLOSED when the goal row cannot be read",
        "lets a drain-fleet goal clear to defaults or go unlimited",
        "binds the holder-policy merge door too, since it writes through the same writer",
        "resolves the goal from the LAUNCHER and takes no goalId argument",
        "resolves the INHERITED goal for a launcher that merely works under one",
        "is inert with no goal in scope — no ceiling, no profile, not degraded",
        "readGoalLaunchSettingsForLauncher degrades with a reason instead of throwing",
        "resolveGoalLaunch degrades instead of throwing, and imposes no ceiling",
        "resolveGoalLaunch still THROWS for a superseded holder",
        "readGoalLaunchSettingsForLauncher still THROWS for a superseded holder",
        "a LIVE handoff is not superseded — the predecessor still resolves its goal",
        "COMPOSES: a fleet with room is still refused when the GOAL is full",
        "rubricStewardship:'skip' omits the stewardship read even for a goal with rubric duties (EI-25306440159635835)",
        "skips a blocked first worklist plan and emits the next eligible launch",
        "blocks launch deterministically when the worklist plan identity is unresolved",
        "assembles the portfolio only for the GOAL-holder launch slot",
        "surfaces missing owner, link criterion and goal stamps as typed issues",
